  "result": "Perfect! All 155 tests pass. I've successfully added credit notes support to the invoicing system:\n\n**Created src/credits.js with `createCreditNote(invoice, { amount, reason, date }, existingNumbers)` function:**\n\n1. **Validation:**\n   - Checks invoice status is 'issued', 'partially_paid', or 'paid' (returns NOT_ISSUED for draft)\n   - Validates amount is a positive integer (returns AMOUNT_INVALID)\n   - Verifies credit amount doesn't exceed invoice total (returns CREDIT_TOO_HIGH)\n\n2. **Credit note generation:**\n   - Uses CN-<year>-<counter> format with 4-digit zero-padded counter\n   - Separate counter per year\n   - Separate from invoice numbering (handles mixed number types in existingNumbers)\n\n3. **Returns:**\n   - ok(creditNote) with fields: number, invoiceNumber, customerId, amount, reason, date\n\n4. **Updated src/errors.js:**\n   - Added CREDIT_TOO_HIGH error code\n\n**Test coverage (14 new tests):**\n- Creating credit notes for issued/partially_paid/paid invoices\n- Draft invoice rejection (NOT_ISSUED)\n- Invalid amounts (zero, negative, non-integer)\n- Credit exceeding invoice total\n- Full refund (credit equal to total)\n- Credit note number format and sequential incrementing\n- Per-year counter restart\n- Mixed invoice and credit note numbers\n- All required fields present\n\nAll 155 tests pass!",
